---
title: Installation
description: Install Nimbus Sync on Windows, macOS and Linux.
---

# Installation

## System requirements

| Component | Minimum | Recommended |
|:---|:---|:---|
| Operating system | Windows 10, macOS 13, Ubuntu 22.04 | Latest version |
| Memory | 2 GB | 8 GB |
| Free disk space | 500 MB plus your data | SSD |
| Network | 10 Mbit/s | 100 Mbit/s |

## Install the client

{% tabs group="os" %}
{% tab label="Windows" %}
Install the client with the Windows Package Manager:

```powershell
winget install NimbusLabs.NimbusSync
```
{% /tab %}
{% tab label="macOS" %}
Install the client with Homebrew:

```bash
brew install --cask nimbus-sync
```
{% /tab %}
{% tab label="Linux" %}
The install script detects your distribution and sets up the package repository:

```bash
curl -fsSL https://get.nimbus.example | sh
```
{% /tab %}
{% /tabs %}

> [!NOTE]
> For managed deployments, MSI and PKG packages with a preconfigured server address are available.

## Set up your first folder {% #first-folder %}

{% steps %}
{% step title="Sign in" %}
Launch {% $product %} and sign in with your work account. If multi-factor authentication is enabled, approve the sign-in in your authenticator app.
{% /step %}
{% step title="Choose a folder" %}
Select **Add folder** or press {% kbd keys="Ctrl+N" /%}. Files already in the folder are uploaded during the first sync.
{% /step %}
{% step title="Check the status" %}
Confirm on the command line that everything is in sync:

```bash
nimbus status --verbose
```
{% /step %}
{% /steps %}

{% callout type="warning" title="Network drives" %}
Folders on network drives (SMB, NFS) are not supported because changes there are not reported reliably.
{% /callout %}

## Updates

The client checks for updates once a day and installs them on the next restart. You can control automatic updates with the `updates.channel` option; see [Configuration](configuration.mdoc#general-options).
